BCR adjustments to icu4c/source/common/BUILD.bazel for building with cl.exe / clang-cl
(static library build, MSVC CRT). Applied after the base patch for this file.

* /utf-8 copts: these targets compile sources holding UTF-8 char literals
  (currency symbols in static_unicode_sets.h, fullwidth letters in
  uchar.cpp, case-mapping tables in ustrcase.cpp, Greek letters in
  alphaindex.cpp). Without /utf-8 cl.exe reads the file as the ANSI code
  page and rejects the literals with C2015 "too many characters in
  constant". GCC/clang/MinGW read UTF-8 by default and are unaffected.

* U_STATIC_IMPLEMENTATION in `defines` on :headers: propagated to every
  consumer so icu's public headers stop emitting __declspec(dllimport)
  references that a static link cannot satisfy (LNK4217 / LNK1120).

* :platform linkopts: putil.cpp's uprv_detectWindowsTimeZone reads the
  registry (RegOpenKeyExW and friends, advapi32.lib), which the MSVC
  toolchain does not link by default. Mirrors the -ldl entry for Linux.

* :platform deps: the base patch globs udata.cpp into :platform, and
  udata.cpp references the data entry point (icudt<NN>_dat) that
  //icu4c/source/stubdata defines. Upstream's :udata target carries that
  dep; :platform must too now that it owns the source, otherwise binaries
  that link :platform without :udata (gennorm2, genprops) fail with
  LNK2001 on MSVC, whose linker pulls udata.obj in for other symbols.

Targets touched: :headers, :platform, :uchar, :ustring_case.

--- a/icu4c/source/common/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/icu4c/source/common/BUILD.bazel
@@ -22,6 +22,11 @@
 
 cc_library(
     name = "headers",
+    defines = select({
+        "@rules_cc//cc/compiler:clang-cl": ["U_STATIC_IMPLEMENTATION"],
+        "@rules_cc//cc/compiler:msvc-cl": ["U_STATIC_IMPLEMENTATION"],
+        "//conditions:default": [],
+    }),
     hdrs = glob([
         "unicode/*.h", # public
         "*.h",         # internal
@@ -43,11 +48,17 @@
 
